<title>VIETNAM: Ford sees breaking even in Vietnam by 2000.</title>
<headline>Ford sees breaking even in Vietnam by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. auto giant Ford Motor Company, said on Friday it expects to break even on its investment in Vietnam by 2000 despite what analysts say is an overcrowded market.</p>
<p>Ford's executive vice president, Wayne Booker, dismissed industry concerns over problems facing manufacturers in Vietnam and said the company's first locally made vehicle would roll off the production line within a year.</p>
</text>
